<%# One hypothesis of the open-endedness finding: the verdict its own sweep supports, then
    the arm-by-arm counts it was read from. `reading` names the deciding observable and
    `unit` what it is measured in, so the same table serves a length and a lineage count. %>
<p>
  <span class="badge <%= bet.badge_class %>"><%= bet.verdict_label %></span>
  <strong>
    <% if bet.verdict == :supported %>
      <%= safe_join(bet.raising_arms.map { |arm| tag.span(arm.label, class: "mono") }, ", ") %>
      settles above the control arm in most of its runs.
    <% elsif bet.verdict == :not_supported %>
      No arm settles above the control arm in most of its runs — the refutation condition
      of the hypothesis, at the seeds this sweep has.
    <% else %>
      Not enough transitioned seeds to decide it either way.
    <% end %>
  </strong>
  <% if bet.experiment? %>
    <%= link_to bet.experiment.name, experiment_path(bet.experiment) %> has
    <%= pluralize bet.transitioned_count, "transitioned run" %>, <%= bet.measured_count %> of
    them carrying <%= reading %> after the crossing.
  <% else %>
    The sweep <span class="mono"><%= bet.slug %></span> is not in this database, so it has
    no runs behind it here.
  <% end %>
  <% if bet.resolved? %>
    The control arm's median is
    <%= number_with_precision bet.control_median, precision: 1, strip_insignificant_zeros: true %>
    <%= unit %>, and every other arm with at least
    <%= pluralize Findings::OpenEndednessSurvey::MIN_ARM_RUNS, "measured run" %> is counted
    against it.
  <% else %>
    A verdict needs at least
    <%= pluralize Findings::OpenEndednessSurvey::MIN_ARM_RUNS, "measured run" %> in the
    control arm and in one other arm; until then the hypothesis is untested rather than
    refuted.
  <% end %>
</p>

<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" id="<%= bet.slug %>-<%= bet.decided_by %>-arms"
     aria-label="Arms of the <%= bet.slug %> sweep, against its control arm">
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Arm</th>
        <th class="numeric">Transitioned runs</th>
        <th class="numeric">Measured</th>
        <th class="numeric">Median <%= unit %></th>
        <th class="numeric">Above control</th>
        <th class="numeric">Still rising</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% bet.arms.each do |arm| %>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <span class="mono"><%= arm.label %></span>
            <% if arm.control? %><span class="badge badge-info">control</span><% end %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.transitioned_count %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.measured_count(bet.decided_by) %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono">
            <% median = arm.median_plateau(bet.decided_by) %>
            <%= median ? number_with_precision(median, precision: 1, strip_insignificant_zeros: true) : "—" %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono">
            <%= arm.control? ? "—" : arm.above_count(bet.decided_by, bet.control_median) %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.rising_count(bet.decided_by) %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="text-sm text-muted">
  One row per arm of the sweep. "Measured" counts the transitioned runs whose samples carry
  the reading after their own crossing; the median is of each run's highest post-crossing
  reading, the plateau it settled at. "Above control" counts the runs of the arm whose
  plateau is strictly above the control arm's median, and "Still rising" the runs whose last
  reading is above their first.
</p>
